  "facts": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Nances Creek is a close‑knit community in Calhoun County, Alabama, surrounded by rolling hills and farmland in the foothills of the Appalachian Mountains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://nancescreekfarms.com/explore-area.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community grew around farms, churches and schools that served families scattered along the creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://nancescreekfarms.com/explore-area.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Stories differ on how Nances Creek got its name: some say it honors an early settler, others connect it to a local Creek leader known as Chief Nance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://nancescreekfarms.com/explore-area.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Today, Nances Creek sits between Jacksonville and Piedmont, offering easy access to trails, creeks, and mountain views while keeping its quiet, rural character.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://nancescreekfarms.com/explore-area.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "While we don't have a date for the founding of Nances Creek, you might consider that their post office opened in 1891.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
